# Carbon Black Lucene Rule

*Detection rule · `rule::1.0` · version 1 · modified 2026-01-02 · TLP:CLEAR*

Simulated Carbon Black rule for CLI E2E corpus.

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Severity | High |
| Detection model | [Credential Access Objective](../objectives/credential-access-objective.md) |
| ATT&CK | [`T1059`](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059) Command and Scripting Interpreter |
| Platforms | Carbon Black Cloud: `STAGING` (PREVIEW runs) |

**On this page:** [Deployment](#deployment) · [Platform configuration](#platform-configuration) · [Response](#response) · [ATT&CK techniques](#att-ck-techniques) · [Detection coverage](#detection-coverage) · [Metadata](#metadata)

## Deployment

What `opentide deploy` does with this rule: each platform block's status, the runs that act on it, and the tenants they reach.

| Platform | Status | Deployed by | Tenants | Block enabled |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Carbon Black Cloud | `STAGING` | PREVIEW runs | no tenant configured | yes |

- `STAGING` (strategy `PREVIEW`): Deployed in staging environment for operational testing

> **Warning:** Carbon Black Cloud configures no tenant: a run that deploys this block fails until one is added to the platform file.

